  "agent": {
    "note": "Iter 7 — addressing iter6 feedback. (a) Avatar shrunk from 80×100 to 40×40 so the message body dominates the row height. (b) Body widened from 470 → 600px (per \"both message slots can take a bit more width\"). (c) Avatars now carry a circular SVG mask via the new circleMask() helper in @m0saic/dsl-stdlib/libraries/mask-shapes — flip on Masks in the editor VIEW panel to see the silhouette. The agent now has a reusable circle-mask primitive (also pillMask + roundedRectMask in the same module) so this stops being something to re-derive every iteration. (d) Human bubbles use brand orange (#EF7525) matching Momo's user bubble convention; agent bubbles use a subtle dark (#23262f) so they read against the bg without competing with the orange. (e) Background set to #14151b — same color Layout uses for its topbar, so the chat sits in the familiar Mosaic Desktop palette.",
    "question": "How does the brand orange feel for human bubbles? Is the 40×40 avatar circle right, or do you want it bigger / smaller? The agent dark bubble (#23262f) — too subtle (almost vanishes into bg)? Should the system row use one of the brand accent colors instead of neutral gray? Anything else feel off — y-spacing, body width, row stride?",
    "context": {
